Context from Costpoint — Contract W91278-20-D-0067, Task Order 0003:
Contract type: T&M | Awarded: Mar 2020 | Task Order 0003 issued: Jun 2022 | Current mod: P00012 (pending, equitable adjustment request). Applicable DFARS edition at award: DFARS 252.243-7002 (Dec 2018). Current DFARS edition: DFARS 252.243-7002 (Jan 2024 revision).

**SharePoint — /proposals/W91278/TO3/cost-narrative-P00012.docx (last modified Mar 3, 2025):**
Section 3 — Equitable Adjustment Basis:
'Sentinel requests equitable adjustment of $487,200 for the directed scope change under CLIN 0003AA. Labor rates applied per the task order's negotiated ceiling rates. Indirect rates applied: FY24 provisional billing rates per DCMA-approved forward pricing rate agreement (FPRA) dated Nov 2024.'

**Email — Subject: 'W91278 TO3 — EA Cost Methodology Question' (Mar 10, 2025)**
From: capt.morrison@us.army.mil
To: pat.holloway@sentineldef.com

Ms. Holloway — We're reviewing your EA proposal. Question: you applied FY24 indirect rates, but the changes clause incorporated at contract award references the Dec 2018 DFARS language. Under that version, the equitable adjustment should use rates 'in effect at the time the work was performed.' The directed change occurred in Aug 2024; can you confirm whether the Aug 2024 actual rates or the FY24 FPRA rates are more appropriate?

— Capt. Morrison, ACO

**Teams — #sentinel-cost-accounting (Mar 11, 2025, 10:30 AM)**
@pat.holloway: Linda — got a question from the ACO on W91278 TO3. They're asking whether we should use actuals or FPRA rates for the EA. DFARS version at award says 'rates in effect at time work performed.'
@linda.castellano: For a T&M, the ceiling rates on the schedule cap your direct labor. Indirects should be actuals for work already performed, FPRA for forward pricing.
@pat.holloway: But the EA spans Aug-Dec 2024. Some work performed, some forward.
@linda.castellano: Then bifurcate. Aug-Nov use actuals (we have those final now), Dec forward use FPRA.
@pat.holloway: Got it. But wait — our FY24 actuals came in LOWER than FPRA. $487K was built on FPRA throughout.
@linda.castellano: :eyes:
@pat.holloway: Yeah. If we bifurcate, the number drops to maybe $461K.
@linda.castellano: You already submitted at $487K?
@pat.holloway: Submitted last week.
@linda.castellano: You'll need to self-correct before they catch it. CAS 401 consistency issue if you don't.
[Thread ends]

**Costpoint — Indirect Rate Summary FY2024:**
FPRA rates (approved Nov 2024): Fringe 38.2% | OH 64.1% | G&A 12.8%
Actual rates (final, certified Feb 2025): Fringe 37.9% | OH 61.3% | G&A 12.4%

**GovWin — Contract Notes (internal):**
W91278-20-D-0067: 'NOTE — Dec 2018 DFARS changes clause applies. Do NOT cite Jan 2024 revision language in any mods. PCO confirmed in Apr 2023 telecon that contract will not be bilaterally modified to incorporate later DFARS revisions.'
